{
  "summary": "The V1 specification from round 3 is nearly implementation-ready but has two remaining blind spots worth flagging. First, the proposed extraction of the 'last history entry whose note contains review-stage content' is underspecified and fragile — history entries are free-text notes like 'Starting round 2 (claude/opus)' with no structured stage tag, so filtering by 'review-stage content' requires pattern-matching on strings that may change without notice. V1 should simplify to extracting only `plan_exploration_summary` and `impl_notes` — two concrete, always-present fields — and skip the history-mining entirely. Review feedback is not reliably capturable without schema changes, and pretending it is will produce either empty extractions or false matches. Second, the proposal says `_prepend_context()` should 'iterate over config.boards' to include board context, but this is wrong — the runner processes a single feature at a time, which belongs to exactly one board. Iterating over all boards would prepend irrelevant context from unrelated boards into the prompt. The correct approach is to pass the feature's board name (available from the FeatureFile being processed) into `_prepend_context()` and read only that board's BOARD_CONTEXT.md. This is a one-parameter change to the method signature, not an iteration pattern. Both issues are small but would produce bugs if implemented as currently specified."
}
